Hirvonen2017323,Neural network metamodelling in multi-objective optimization of a high latitude solar community,doe,1,6,pdf,2,no,no,"Instead of generating a complete training set before optimization, the optimization is started with a very small training set which is updated as the optimization progresses. The ANN is retrained as new samples are added after each optimization step, increasing the ANN accuracy and improving optimization results. Additionally, instead of a single neural network for the whole search space, several neural networks are trained in parallel, each representing a different section of the objective space."
Hirvonen2017323,Neural network metamodelling in multi-objective optimization of a high latitude solar community,doe,2,3,pdf,2,no,no,"One metamodelling technique is the use of artiﬁcial neural networks (ANN). The principles of ANN are explained in detail in Kalogirou (2000) . In short, neural net- works use linear equations to ﬁnd relations between inputs and outputs and can be used to quickly simulate even phenomena that are not completely understood, as long as proper training data is available."
Hirvonen2017323,Neural network metamodelling in multi-objective optimization of a high latitude solar community,doe,3,3,pdf,2,no,no,"The principles of ANN are explained in detail in Kalogirou (2000) . In short, neural net- works use linear equations to ﬁnd relations between inputs and outputs and can be used to quickly simulate even phenomena that are not completely understood, as long as proper training data is available. For example, ANN was used to make a metamodel out of a TRNSYS building model, which was then used with a genetic algo- rithm (GA) to do optimization ( Asadi et al., 2014 )."
Hirvonen2017323,Neural network metamodelling in multi-objective optimization of a high latitude solar community,doe,4,3,pdf,2,no,no,"In short, neural net- works use linear equations to ﬁnd relations between inputs and outputs and can be used to quickly simulate even phenomena that are not completely understood, as long as proper training data is available. For example, ANN was used to make a metamodel out of a TRNSYS building model, which was then used with a genetic algo- rithm (GA) to do optimization ( Asadi et al., 2014 ). First, parametric runs were done to generate a database for training the ANN."
Hirvonen2017323,Neural network metamodelling in multi-objective optimization of a high latitude solar community,doe,5,3,pdf,2,no,no,"First, parametric runs were done to generate a database for training the ANN. The ANN metamodel is very fast to use and allows quick optimization. Unfortunately, generating an adequate training set to ensure the accuracy of the metamodel requires a signiﬁcant amount of simu- lations, so actual time saving compared to direct optimization is not guaranteed."
Hirvonen2017323,Neural network metamodelling in multi-objective optimization of a high latitude solar community,doe,6,3,pdf,2,no,no,"The ANN metamodel is very fast to use and allows quick optimization. Unfortunately, generating an adequate training set to ensure the accuracy of the metamodel requires a signiﬁcant amount of simu- lations, so actual time saving compared to direct optimization is not guaranteed. Generally neural networks are trained with an extensive dataset and then used to completely replace the original model to complete optimization, as was done in Boukelia et al. (2016) and Magnier and Haghighat (2010) ."
Hirvonen2017323,Neural network metamodelling in multi-objective optimization of a high latitude solar community,doe,7,3,pdf,2,no,yes,"However, other meth- ods such as kriging have also been used for parallel optimization and surrogate modeling ( Hussein and Deb, 2016 ). The novelty in this study is the introduction of a new neural network based optimization method for problems where the func- tion evaluation takes a long time compared to other calculation processes. Instead of generating a complete training set before optimization, the optimization is started with a very small training set which is updated as the optimization progresses."
Hirvonen2017323,Neural network metamodelling in multi-objective optimization of a high latitude solar community,doe,8,3,pdf,2,no,yes,"The novelty in this study is the introduction of a new neural network based optimization method for problems where the func- tion evaluation takes a long time compared to other calculation processes. Instead of generating a complete training set before optimization, the optimization is started with a very small training set which is updated as the optimization progresses. The ANN is retrained as new samples are added after each optimization step, increasing the ANN accuracy and improving optimization results."
Hirvonen2017323,Neural network metamodelling in multi-objective optimization of a high latitude solar community,doe,9,3,pdf,4,no,no,"Instead of a single general neural network, several local neural networks were used. The idea was that neural network accuracy is improved by having to model a smaller range of variables and dealing less with outliers. Instead of generating a complete training set before optimiza- tion, the optimization was started with a very small sample set and an inaccurate neural network model, which was updated as optimization progressed."
Hirvonen2017323,Neural network metamodelling in multi-objective optimization of a high latitude solar community,doe,10,3,pdf,4,no,no,"The idea was that neural network accuracy is improved by having to model a smaller range of variables and dealing less with outliers. Instead of generating a complete training set before optimiza- tion, the optimization was started with a very small sample set and an inaccurate neural network model, which was updated as optimization progressed. After every iteration, the sample set grew and an updated neural network was generated."
Li2023,A novel method of creating machine learning-based time series meta-models for building energy analysis,pattern,1,8,abstract,,no,no,"The meta-models have been widely used to replace computationally expensive engineering-based building energy models for model calibration, sensitivity analysis, and performance optimization of buildings. However, most meta-models are used for monthly or annual building energy analysis applying the same procedure as building energy or load prediction."
Li2023,A novel method of creating machine learning-based time series meta-models for building energy analysis,pattern,2,6,pdf,1,no,no,"A novel method of creating machine learning-based time series meta-models for building energy analysis Guangchen Li a, Wei Tian a,b,⇑, Hu Zhang a, Xing Fu c a Tianjin Key Laboratory of Integrated Design and On-line Monitoring for Light Industry & Food Machinery and Equipment, College of Mechanical Enginee ring, Tianjin University of Science and Technology, China b Tianjin International Joint Research and Development Center of Low-Carbon Green Process Equipment, Tianjin, China c Tianjin Architecture Design Institute, Tianjin, China article info Article history: Received 19 October 2022 Revised 8 December 2022 Accepted 27 December 2022 Available online 29 December 2022 Keywords: Building energy Meta-model Distributed lag model Machine learning Time series model abstract The meta-models have been widely used to replace computationally expensive engineering-based build- ing energy models for model calibration, sensitivity analysis, and performance optimization of buildings. However, most meta-models are used for monthly or annual building energy analysis applying the same procedure as building energy or load prediction."
