Li2023,A novel method of creating machine learning-based time series meta-models for building energy analysis,pattern,4,6,pdf,8,no,no,"The learning models are used for the meta-models to replace computationally expensive engineering-based models. Hence, computational time is a very important performance indicator, which is different from the conventional time-series energy/load prediction of buildings. Table 3 The optimal tuning parameters from ten lag-free machine learning models."
Li2023,A novel method of creating machine learning-based time series meta-models for building energy analysis,pattern,5,4,pdf,2,no,no,"The meta-models can approximate complex relationships among inputs and outputs in dynamic physics-based energy mod- els of buildings. A good balance should be obtained between com- putational cost and model accuracy for meta-models. In the ﬁeld of building energy analysis, the meta-models can be used for uncer- tainty analysis [8], model calibration [9], sensitivity analysis [10], performance optimization [11], and model predictive control [12]."
Li2023,A novel method of creating machine learning-based time series meta-models for building energy analysis,pattern,6,4,pdf,2,no,no,"A good balance should be obtained between com- putational cost and model accuracy for meta-models. In the ﬁeld of building energy analysis, the meta-models can be used for uncer- tainty analysis [8], model calibration [9], sensitivity analysis [10], performance optimization [11], and model predictive control [12]. For two-dimensional Monte Carlo uncertainty analysis, the meta-models should be used to replace computational expensive energy models since a large number of simulation runs are involved (over millions of simulations in [8])."
Li2023,A novel method of creating machine learning-based time series meta-models for building energy analysis,pattern,7,4,pdf,2,no,no,"In the ﬁeld of building energy analysis, the meta-models can be used for uncer- tainty analysis [8], model calibration [9], sensitivity analysis [10], performance optimization [11], and model predictive control [12]. For two-dimensional Monte Carlo uncertainty analysis, the meta-models should be used to replace computational expensive energy models since a large number of simulation runs are involved (over millions of simulations in [8]). The meta-model is a common method to reduce computational cost in model calibra- tion since there are over 100,000 simulation runs required to reach the convergence of MCMC results [13]."
Li2023,A novel method of creating machine learning-based time series meta-models for building energy analysis,pattern,8,4,pdf,21,no,no,"Besides, the building hourly meta-model can also reduce the energy consumption of building operations while ensuring the thermal comfort of indoor occupants by optimizing multiple target parameters, such as HVAC set-point temperature, lamp, and equipment utilization rate [57,58]. The application of meta-models for building performance optimization has the advantage of signiﬁcant time savings over physical simula- tion models. Conclusion This paper explores the construction of fast and accurate time- series meta-models to replace the engineering-based building energy model."
