Sami20181416,Thermal properties optimization of microencapsulated a renewable and non-toxic phase change material with a polystyrene shell for thermal energy storage systems,pattern,2,6,pdf,1,no,no,"Research Paper Thermal properties optimization of microencapsulated a renewable and non-toxic phase change material with a polystyrene shell for thermal energy storage systems S. Etesami a a Department of Chemical Engineering, Isfahan University of Technology, P.O. Box: 84156-83111, Isfahan, Iran b Department of Process Engineering, Faculty of Chemical Engineering, Tarbiat Modares University, Tehran, Iran highlights /C15 Microencapsulated of lauric acid with a polystyrene shell was prepared. /C15 A renewable and non-toxic phase change materials has been used for the process. /C15 Emulsion polymerization has been applied as a microencapsulated technique. /C15 Response surface method was applied to the statistical design. /C15 The microencapsulated PCM had a good potential for energy storage system. article info Article history: Received 12 September 2017 Revised 5 November 2017 Accepted 23 November 2017 Available online 24 November 2017 Keywords: Lauric acid Renewable Phase Change Material (PCM) Microencapsulation Response Surface Methodology (RSM) Process optimization Emulsion polymerization abstract Thermal energy storage (TES) plays an important role in the development of an efﬁcient solar energy sys- tem by storing the solar energy when available during the daytime and use it at night when required."
