Guo20222057,Training Deep Neural Network for Optimal Power Allocation in Islanded Microgrid Systems: A Distributed Learning-Based Approach,doe,1,11,pdf,5,yes,no,"Note that all the training data have been normalized into [− 1, 1] and the corresponding normalization is also applied to the testing data. 2) Training and V alidation Stage: We ﬁrst use the training data set to optimize the weights of the DNN so that it gradually approaches our desired output. The cost function we use is the mean square error (MSE) between label {P∗ i (k)} and the output of the DNN."
Guo20222057,Training Deep Neural Network for Optimal Power Allocation in Islanded Microgrid Systems: A Distributed Learning-Based Approach,doe,2,8,pdf,5,yes,no,"2) Training and V alidation Stage: We ﬁrst use the training data set to optimize the weights of the DNN so that it gradually approaches our desired output. The cost function we use is the mean square error (MSE) between label {P∗ i (k)} and the output of the DNN. The optimization algorithm utilized for training here is Adam, which is most commonly used in deep learning recently [34]."
Guo20222057,Training Deep Neural Network for Optimal Power Allocation in Islanded Microgrid Systems: A Distributed Learning-Based Approach,doe,3,7,pdf,5,no,no,"According to the co mmon practice in neural network training [22], we randomly divide the data set into a training set, a validation set, and a test set at a ratio of 5: 2:3. Note that all the training data have been normalized into [− 1, 1] and the corresponding normalization is also applied to the testing data. 2) Training and V alidation Stage: We ﬁrst use the training data set to optimize the weights of the DNN so that it gradually approaches our desired output."
Guo20222057,Training Deep Neural Network for Optimal Power Allocation in Islanded Microgrid Systems: A Distributed Learning-Based Approach,doe,4,4,pdf,5,no,no,"It is worth mentioning that the range of training set should cover all the possible values of P d , so that in the subsequent online applica- tion stage, there is no need to worry about the generalization performance of the well-trai ned DNN. Repeating running the HDO algorithm with arbitrary distinct load demand P(k) d , we can ﬁnally get the entire data set {((Pd/N)(k), P∗ i (k))}K k=1 for the i th DG. According to the co mmon practice in neural network training [22], we randomly divide the data set into a training set, a validation set, and a test set at a ratio of 5: 2:3."
Guo20222057,Training Deep Neural Network for Optimal Power Allocation in Islanded Microgrid Systems: A Distributed Learning-Based Approach,doe,5,4,pdf,5,no,no,"Repeating running the HDO algorithm with arbitrary distinct load demand P(k) d , we can ﬁnally get the entire data set {((Pd/N)(k), P∗ i (k))}K k=1 for the i th DG. According to the co mmon practice in neural network training [22], we randomly divide the data set into a training set, a validation set, and a test set at a ratio of 5: 2:3. Note that all the training data have been normalized into [− 1, 1] and the corresponding normalization is also applied to the testing data."
Guo20222057,Training Deep Neural Network for Optimal Power Allocation in Islanded Microgrid Systems: A Distributed Learning-Based Approach,doe,6,3,pdf,5,no,no,"The obtained optimal power output P∗ i (k), i = 1,..., N together with its corresponding average load demand (Pd/N)(k) constitute the kth training sample. It is worth mentioning that the range of training set should cover all the possible values of P d , so that in the subsequent online applica- tion stage, there is no need to worry about the generalization performance of the well-trai ned DNN. Repeating running the HDO algorithm with arbitrary distinct load demand P(k) d , we can ﬁnally get the entire data set {((Pd/N)(k), P∗ i (k))}K k=1 for the i th DG."
Guo20222057,Training Deep Neural Network for Optimal Power Allocation in Islanded Microgrid Systems: A Distributed Learning-Based Approach,doe,7,3,pdf,5,no,no,"Algorithm Implementation The proposed distributed learning-based optimization algo- rithm can be implemented and calculate the optimal power output for each DG in real-time, once the off-line training of the DNN network completes. To validate the effectiveness of our proposed scheme, several case studies will be provided in the next section. Remark 4: The proposed distributed learning-based OP A algorithm distinguishes from tra ditional numerical optimiza- tion approaches in the following aspects: 1) no new mathe- matical derivation of the optimization algorithm is required, as we can use the well-established algorithm to generate the training data set."
Guo20222057,Training Deep Neural Network for Optimal Power Allocation in Islanded Microgrid Systems: A Distributed Learning-Based Approach,doe,8,3,pdf,5,no,no,"To validate the effectiveness of our proposed scheme, several case studies will be provided in the next section. Remark 4: The proposed distributed learning-based OP A algorithm distinguishes from tra ditional numerical optimiza- tion approaches in the following aspects: 1) no new mathe- matical derivation of the optimization algorithm is required, as we can use the well-established algorithm to generate the training data set. Instead, we can immediately get P ∗ i by feeding (Pd(t)/N) into the well-trained DNN network, where just some simple matrix calculations are manipulated; 2) the DNN-based method is a purely data-driven approach."
Guo20222057,Training Deep Neural Network for Optimal Power Allocation in Islanded Microgrid Systems: A Distributed Learning-Based Approach,doe,9,3,pdf,5,no,no,"Remark 4: The proposed distributed learning-based OP A algorithm distinguishes from tra ditional numerical optimiza- tion approaches in the following aspects: 1) no new mathe- matical derivation of the optimization algorithm is required, as we can use the well-established algorithm to generate the training data set. Instead, we can immediately get P ∗ i by feeding (Pd(t)/N) into the well-trained DNN network, where just some simple matrix calculations are manipulated; 2) the DNN-based method is a purely data-driven approach. If these optimal power outputs and corresponding load demand data are available, we even do not require to know the coefﬁcients of cost functions in (1); and 3) the most signiﬁcant advantage of the learning-based approach over traditional numerical opti- mization algorithms is that it requires less time to obtain the optimal solution online, which is quite suitable for real-time optimization."
