Jahangiri20244849,A machine learning approach to analysis of Canadian provincial power system decarbonization,pattern,9,3,pdf,2,no,no,"Provincial level analyses could provide planners and policymakers with in-depth understanding of the chal - lenges and opportunities specific to each province, while producing deeper insights into policies for developing variable renewable genera - tion, reducing emissions from natural gas generation, and expanding interprovincial transmission. The historic focus on pathway analysis also lends itself to electricity system modeling centered on least-cost optimization, simulation, and single-factor sensitivity. This conventional approach has limitations relevant to evaluating net-zero pathway robustness, which requires comprehensive examination of strategies and technologies in the context of uncertainties inherent to evolving and interconnected power systems."
