Hu2021671,A Bayesian Approach for Estimating Uncertainty in Stochastic Economic Dispatch Considering Wind Power Penetration,pattern,1,14,pdf,1,yes,no,"1, JANUARY 2021 671 A Bayesian Approach for Estimating Uncertainty in Stochastic Economic Dispatch Considering Wind Power Penetration Zhixiong Hu , Yijun Xu , Member , IEEE,M e r tK o r k a l i, Senior Member , IEEE,X i a oC h e n , Lamine Mili , Life Fellow, IEEE, and Jaber V alinejad, Student Member , IEEE Abstract—The increasing penetration of renewable energy re- sources in power systems, represented as random processes, con- verts the traditional deterministic economic dispatch problem into a stochastic one. To estimate the uncertainty in the stochastic economic dispatch (SED) problem for the purpose of forecasting, the conventional Monte-Carlo (MC) method is prohibitively time- consuming for practical applications. To overcome this problem, we propose a novel Gaussian-process-emulator (GPE)-based ap- proach to quantify the uncertainty in SED considering wind power penetration."
Hu2021671,A Bayesian Approach for Estimating Uncertainty in Stochastic Economic Dispatch Considering Wind Power Penetration,pattern,2,13,abstract,,yes,no,"The increasing penetration of renewable energy resources in power systems, represented as random processes, converts the traditional deterministic economic dispatch problem into a stochastic one. To estimate the uncertainty in the stochastic economic dispatch (SED) problem for the purpose of forecasting, the conventional Monte-Carlo (MC) method is prohibitively time-consuming for practical applications. To overcome this problem, we propose a novel Gaussian-process-emulator (GPE)-based approach to quantify the uncertainty in SED considering wind power penetration."
Hu2021671,A Bayesian Approach for Estimating Uncertainty in Stochastic Economic Dispatch Considering Wind Power Penetration,pattern,3,10,abstract,,yes,no,"To estimate the uncertainty in the stochastic economic dispatch (SED) problem for the purpose of forecasting, the conventional Monte-Carlo (MC) method is prohibitively time-consuming for practical applications. To overcome this problem, we propose a novel Gaussian-process-emulator (GPE)-based approach to quantify the uncertainty in SED considering wind power penetration. Facing high-dimensional real-world data representing the correlated uncertainties from wind generation, a manifold-learning-based Isomap algorithm is proposed to efficiently represent the low-dimensional hidden probabilistic structure of the data."
Hu2021671,A Bayesian Approach for Estimating Uncertainty in Stochastic Economic Dispatch Considering Wind Power Penetration,pattern,4,9,pdf,1,no,no,"IEEE TRANSACTIONS ON SUSTAINABLE ENERGY , VOL. 1, JANUARY 2021 671 A Bayesian Approach for Estimating Uncertainty in Stochastic Economic Dispatch Considering Wind Power Penetration Zhixiong Hu , Yijun Xu , Member , IEEE,M e r tK o r k a l i, Senior Member , IEEE,X i a oC h e n , Lamine Mili , Life Fellow, IEEE, and Jaber V alinejad, Student Member , IEEE Abstract—The increasing penetration of renewable energy re- sources in power systems, represented as random processes, con- verts the traditional deterministic economic dispatch problem into a stochastic one. To estimate the uncertainty in the stochastic economic dispatch (SED) problem for the purpose of forecasting, the conventional Monte-Carlo (MC) method is prohibitively time- consuming for practical applications."
