Hu2021671,A Bayesian Approach for Estimating Uncertainty in Stochastic Economic Dispatch Considering Wind Power Penetration,pattern,6,8,pdf,10,yes,no,"If we use x11 and x12 to distinguish xi1 in #SE1 and #SE2, the joint samples of x11,x 12 can be gained by two steps: 1) Sample x11 from its KDE estimated density function 2) Sample x12 ∼N ( ˆβ0 +x11 ˆβ1, ˆσ2), where ˆβ0, ˆβ1, ˆσ2 are estimated intercept, slope, and mean squared error from the results of linear regression between x12 and x11, respectively. A yet another way to deal with correlations between #SE1 and #SE2 is to simply concatenate two 24-dimensional wind data together and use our GPE-Isomap method on the 48- dimensional concatenated data. Hedman, “Wind power dispatch margin for ﬂexible energy and reserve scheduling with in- creased wind generation,” IEEE Trans."
