Karamichailidou20212137,Wind turbine power curve modeling using radial basis function neural networks and tabu search,pattern,1,4,pdf,6,no,no,"Tabu search e non symmetric fuzzy means (TS-NSFM) algorithm 4.1. Standard tabu search Along with different approaches that ﬁnd application in the context of metaheuristic methods, such as genetic algorithms and particle swarm optimization, TS has also been designed to avoid being trapped in local optima by using heuristics to explore the so- lution space beyond local optimality. Its popularity has signi ﬁcantly grown during the last decades, as it is characterized as the most efﬁcient method for handling large scale optimization problems [45]."
Karamichailidou20212137,Wind turbine power curve modeling using radial basis function neural networks and tabu search,pattern,2,4,pdf,6,no,no,"Standard tabu search Along with different approaches that ﬁnd application in the context of metaheuristic methods, such as genetic algorithms and particle swarm optimization, TS has also been designed to avoid being trapped in local optima by using heuristics to explore the so- lution space beyond local optimality. Its popularity has signi ﬁcantly grown during the last decades, as it is characterized as the most efﬁcient method for handling large scale optimization problems [45]. TS can be thought as an iterative descent method, starting with a randomly generated initial solution and examining the neighbor- hood around it."
Karamichailidou20212137,Wind turbine power curve modeling using radial basis function neural networks and tabu search,pattern,3,3,pdf,14,no,no,"However, due to the fact that power generation by a wind turbine depends on various factors besides wind speed, it is reasonable for the ANN models to produce higher accuracy. This advantage gained by the ANN models in terms of accuracy when compared to cubic spline interpolation and the parametric model, is signi ﬁcant enough to justify the considerable increase in computational times needed by the formers. This in- crease can be attributed to the fact that both cubic spline interpo- lation and the parametric model use much simpler algorithms for ﬁtting compared to the ANNs, while they do not involve any structure optimization procedure."
Karamichailidou20212137,Wind turbine power curve modeling using radial basis function neural networks and tabu search,pattern,4,3,pdf,14,no,no,"This advantage gained by the ANN models in terms of accuracy when compared to cubic spline interpolation and the parametric model, is signi ﬁcant enough to justify the considerable increase in computational times needed by the formers. This in- crease can be attributed to the fact that both cubic spline interpo- lation and the parametric model use much simpler algorithms for ﬁtting compared to the ANNs, while they do not involve any structure optimization procedure. Finally, the manufacturer curve model is inferior to the rest of the power curve modeling techniques in terms of MAE values in the testing subset."
