Liu20242534,More Efficient Energy Management for Hybrid AC/DC Microgrids with Hard Constrained Neural Network-Based Conversion Loss Surrogate Models,doe,3,1,pdf,11,no,no,"2544 IEEE TRANSACTIONS ON SMART GRID, VOL. 3, MAY 2024 TABLE III NEURAL NETWORK PARAMETERS TABLE IV TEST RESULTS OF APPROXIMATION ERRORS AND CALCULATION SPEED FOR DIFFERENT SURROGATE MODELS z0,c = [ pc 500, VDC − 658 77 ] T (64) z0,v = [ pv 200, VDC − 658 77 ] T (65) According to [58], ReLU networks can approximate any continuous function with arbitrarily small errors using only three hidden layers. For each NN model, we ﬁx the number of layers at 3 and tune the number of neurons in each layer based on the baseline model performance on a small subset of the training data."
