Salahinezhad2025,Trade-off analysis for optimal design of trigeneration energy systems integrated with solar and hydrogen subsystems: A novel optimization strategy,pattern,9,9,pdf,20,no,yes,"Additionally, applying the TRS-RSM-LCA methodology to other hybrid systems or in different climatic regions could offer valuable in- sights into regional optimization strategies. Finally, incorporating advanced optimization techniques, such as machine learning algo- rithms, could enhance the accuracy and computational efficiency of the optimization process, providing a more comprehensive approach to sustainable energy system design. Conclusions In conclusion, this paper introduced the transient simulation- response surface method-life cycle assessment (TRS-RSM-LCA) as a groundbreaking optimization strategy for designing combined cooling, heat, and power (CCHP) systems that integrate solar collectors and hydrogen generation subsystems."
Salahinezhad2025,Trade-off analysis for optimal design of trigeneration energy systems integrated with solar and hydrogen subsystems: A novel optimization strategy,pattern,10,9,pdf,20,no,no,"Finally, incorporating advanced optimization techniques, such as machine learning algo- rithms, could enhance the accuracy and computational efficiency of the optimization process, providing a more comprehensive approach to sustainable energy system design. Conclusions In conclusion, this paper introduced the transient simulation- response surface method-life cycle assessment (TRS-RSM-LCA) as a groundbreaking optimization strategy for designing combined cooling, heat, and power (CCHP) systems that integrate solar collectors and hydrogen generation subsystems. This innovative approach not only targets the optimal energy, economic, and environmental (3E) perfor- mance of hybrid energy systems over their lifespan but also contributes meaningfully to the broader discourse on sustainable energy solutions."
