alahmad_optimizing_2025,Optimizing renewable energy and green technologies in distribution systems through stochastic planning of distributed energy resources,pattern,3,8,pdf,19,yes,no,"By hybridizing NSGA-II and MOPSO, the algorithm enhances solution quality, convergence speed, and decision-making robustness in multi-objective optimization con- texts. For a detailed step-by-step procedural guide to the successful implementation of the proposed NSGAII-MOPSO-TOPSIS method, readers are encouraged to refer to our recent published works in [59,60,61,25,22,23,21,29] . Results and discussions To rigorously evaluate the efficacy of our proposed planning model, we employ the 69-bus DS, depicted in Fig."
alahmad_optimizing_2025,Optimizing renewable energy and green technologies in distribution systems through stochastic planning of distributed energy resources,pattern,4,8,pdf,29,yes,no,"The charging and discharging behaviour guided by the designed control strategy for each PEV is illustrated in Fig. This visuali- zation demonstrates that the optimized control strategy restricts each PEV ’ s battery to one cycle, effectively preventing battery degradation, extending its lifespan, and postponing the need for EV owners to invest in purchasing new batteries. Conclusions This paper presents a short-term optimization model integrating RDGs, such as wind and PV DGs, PEV-PLs, SBESSs, and MBESSs, aiming to enhance green energy and PEV penetration in the DS."
alahmad_optimizing_2025,Optimizing renewable energy and green technologies in distribution systems through stochastic planning of distributed energy resources,pattern,5,8,pdf,29,yes,no,"This visuali- zation demonstrates that the optimized control strategy restricts each PEV ’ s battery to one cycle, effectively preventing battery degradation, extending its lifespan, and postponing the need for EV owners to invest in purchasing new batteries. Conclusions This paper presents a short-term optimization model integrating RDGs, such as wind and PV DGs, PEV-PLs, SBESSs, and MBESSs, aiming to enhance green energy and PEV penetration in the DS. The model optimizes decision variables, including RDG location and size, and co- ordinates optimal charging and discharging strategies for SBESS-MBESS- PEV and monthly relocation schedules for MBESSs."
alahmad_optimizing_2025,Optimizing renewable energy and green technologies in distribution systems through stochastic planning of distributed energy resources,pattern,6,8,pdf,29,yes,no,"Conclusions This paper presents a short-term optimization model integrating RDGs, such as wind and PV DGs, PEV-PLs, SBESSs, and MBESSs, aiming to enhance green energy and PEV penetration in the DS. The model optimizes decision variables, including RDG location and size, and co- ordinates optimal charging and discharging strategies for SBESS-MBESS- PEV and monthly relocation schedules for MBESSs. The objective is to minimize annual costs, power loss, and voltage deviation."
alahmad_optimizing_2025,Optimizing renewable energy and green technologies in distribution systems through stochastic planning of distributed energy resources,pattern,7,6,pdf,1,no,no,"Optimizing renewable energy and green technologies in distribution systems through stochastic planning of distributed energy resources Ahmad K. ALAhmad a , Renuga Verayiah a , Hussain Shareef b , c , * , Agileswari Ramasamy a , Saleh Ba-swaimi d a Institute of Power Engineering, Universiti Tenaga Nasional (UNITEN), Putrajaya Campus, Jalan IKRAM-UNITEN, 43000 Kajang, Selangor, Malaysia b Department of Electrical and Communication Engineering, College of Engineering, United Arab Emirates University, P.O. Box 15551, Al Ain, the United Arab Emirates c Emirates Center for Mobility Research, United Arab Emirates University, Al Ain, United Arab Emirates. d Department of Electronic and Communications Engineering, College of Engineering & Petroleum, Hadramout University, Mukalla, Yemen ARTICLE INFO Keywords: Renewable energy Collaborative energy planning Distributed generations (DGs) Plug-in electric vehicles (PEVs) Stationary and mobile battery energy storage systems (SBESSs/MBESSs) Power Distribution System Optimization ABSTRACT This paper introduces a short-term stochastic Mixed Integer Non-Linear Programming (MINLP) multi-objective optimization model designed for collaborative planning."
alahmad_optimizing_2025,Optimizing renewable energy and green technologies in distribution systems through stochastic planning of distributed energy resources,pattern,8,6,pdf,1,no,no,"ALAhmad a , Renuga Verayiah a , Hussain Shareef b , c , * , Agileswari Ramasamy a , Saleh Ba-swaimi d a Institute of Power Engineering, Universiti Tenaga Nasional (UNITEN), Putrajaya Campus, Jalan IKRAM-UNITEN, 43000 Kajang, Selangor, Malaysia b Department of Electrical and Communication Engineering, College of Engineering, United Arab Emirates University, P.O. Box 15551, Al Ain, the United Arab Emirates c Emirates Center for Mobility Research, United Arab Emirates University, Al Ain, United Arab Emirates. d Department of Electronic and Communications Engineering, College of Engineering & Petroleum, Hadramout University, Mukalla, Yemen ARTICLE INFO Keywords: Renewable energy Collaborative energy planning Distributed generations (DGs) Plug-in electric vehicles (PEVs) Stationary and mobile battery energy storage systems (SBESSs/MBESSs) Power Distribution System Optimization ABSTRACT This paper introduces a short-term stochastic Mixed Integer Non-Linear Programming (MINLP) multi-objective optimization model designed for collaborative planning. It integrates renewable-based distributed generations (RDGs) like wind and photovoltaic (PV) sources, plug-in electric vehicle parking lots (PEV-PLs), stationary battery energy storage systems (SBESSs), and mobile battery energy storage systems (MBESSs)."
alahmad_optimizing_2025,Optimizing renewable energy and green technologies in distribution systems through stochastic planning of distributed energy resources,pattern,9,6,pdf,1,no,no,"Box 15551, Al Ain, the United Arab Emirates c Emirates Center for Mobility Research, United Arab Emirates University, Al Ain, United Arab Emirates. d Department of Electronic and Communications Engineering, College of Engineering & Petroleum, Hadramout University, Mukalla, Yemen ARTICLE INFO Keywords: Renewable energy Collaborative energy planning Distributed generations (DGs) Plug-in electric vehicles (PEVs) Stationary and mobile battery energy storage systems (SBESSs/MBESSs) Power Distribution System Optimization ABSTRACT This paper introduces a short-term stochastic Mixed Integer Non-Linear Programming (MINLP) multi-objective optimization model designed for collaborative planning. It integrates renewable-based distributed generations (RDGs) like wind and photovoltaic (PV) sources, plug-in electric vehicle parking lots (PEV-PLs), stationary battery energy storage systems (SBESSs), and mobile battery energy storage systems (MBESSs). The main goal is to enhance the penetration of green energy and Plug-in Electric Vehicles (PEVs) within the distribution system (DS)."
alahmad_optimizing_2025,Optimizing renewable energy and green technologies in distribution systems through stochastic planning of distributed energy resources,pattern,10,6,pdf,17,no,no,"Power flow constraints This subsection delineates the mathematical constraints governing power flow dynamics within the system. Ensuring equilibrium, the injected and computed active and reactive power at each bus are equated, meticulously stipulated in (111). The active and reactive power injections at each bus are determined based on the collective contribu- tions from available DSS, wind DGs, PV DGs, PEV-PLs, SBESSs, MBESSs, commercial loads, and residential loads connected to the respective bus, as outlined in (112) and (113). (∀ i ∈ Φ bus , ∀ i ∈ Φ bus , ∀ s ∈ Φ S , t ∈ Φ T , d ∈ Φ D , m ∈ Φ M ) ⎧ ⎨ ⎩ AP injected i , t , s , d , m = AP calculated i , t , s , d , m RP injected i , t , s , d , m = RP calculated i , t , s , d , m (111) Introducing a binary variable in (114) streamlines the process by indicating the availability of each component."
bendriss_novel_2025,A novel improved Frilled Lizard algorithm for solving the optimal planning problem of renewable energy sources within distribution grids under uncertainties,pattern,1,13,pdf,2,no,no,"These studies involve the application of different optimization techniques, encompassing the whale optimization algo- rithm (WOA) [10], the equilibrium optimizer (EO) algorithm [11], the improved wild horse optimization (IWHO) algorithm [12] and the adaptive particle swarm optimization (APSO) [13] to identify the optimal size and site of DGs for reducing power loss. Also, the coyote optimization algorithm (COA) [14] has been applied to find the best site and size of DG units to reduce power loss, lower operating costs, and improve voltage stability. The modified gravitational search algo- rithm (MGSA) [15], the artificial bee colony (ABC) algorithm [3] and the arithmetic optimization algorithm (AOA) [16] have been employed to identify the best site and location of DG units for reducing power losses and elevate the voltage profile."
bendriss_novel_2025,A novel improved Frilled Lizard algorithm for solving the optimal planning problem of renewable energy sources within distribution grids under uncertainties,pattern,2,13,pdf,2,no,no,"The weighted aggregation particle swarm optimization (WAPSO) algorithm was utilized to reduce power losses, enhance voltage stability, and improve network security while account- ing for uncertainties in solar irradiance and wind speed. Hemeida et al. [19], presented a methodology for optimizing DGs placement in power systems considering load uncertainties. The approach utilizes Monte Carlo simulation to generate various load scenarios employing four bio-inspired optimization techniques, namely grey wolf optimiza- tion (GWO), manta ray foraging optimization (MRFO), satin bowerbird optimization (SBO), and whale optimization algorithm (WOA)."
bendriss_novel_2025,A novel improved Frilled Lizard algorithm for solving the optimal planning problem of renewable energy sources within distribution grids under uncertainties,pattern,3,10,pdf,2,no,yes,"In the academic literature, many studies have attempted to solve the optimal planning problem (OPP) of DGs within the RDG, each considering specific objectives, either as a single or multi-objective problem formulation. These studies involve the application of different optimization techniques, encompassing the whale optimization algo- rithm (WOA) [10], the equilibrium optimizer (EO) algorithm [11], the improved wild horse optimization (IWHO) algorithm [12] and the adaptive particle swarm optimization (APSO) [13] to identify the optimal size and site of DGs for reducing power loss. Also, the coyote optimization algorithm (COA) [14] has been applied to find the best site and size of DG units to reduce power loss, lower operating costs, and improve voltage stability."
bendriss_novel_2025,A novel improved Frilled Lizard algorithm for solving the optimal planning problem of renewable energy sources within distribution grids under uncertainties,pattern,4,10,pdf,2,no,no,"Hemeida et al. [19], presented a methodology for optimizing DGs placement in power systems considering load uncertainties. The approach utilizes Monte Carlo simulation to generate various load scenarios employing four bio-inspired optimization techniques, namely grey wolf optimiza- tion (GWO), manta ray foraging optimization (MRFO), satin bowerbird optimization (SBO), and whale optimization algorithm (WOA). The objective was to reduce active power loss, voltage deviation, and maximize the voltage stability index."
bendriss_novel_2025,A novel improved Frilled Lizard algorithm for solving the optimal planning problem of renewable energy sources within distribution grids under uncertainties,pattern,5,10,pdf,2,no,yes,"The approach utilizes Monte Carlo simulation to generate various load scenarios employing four bio-inspired optimization techniques, namely grey wolf optimiza- tion (GWO), manta ray foraging optimization (MRFO), satin bowerbird optimization (SBO), and whale optimization algorithm (WOA). The objective was to reduce active power loss, voltage deviation, and maximize the voltage stability index. In [20], the authors suggested a strategy for allocating PV and battery energy storage systems using a modified Henry gas solubility optimization (HGSO) algorithm to minimize total system power loss, considering PV generation uncer- tainties and time-varying loads."
bendriss_novel_2025,A novel improved Frilled Lizard algorithm for solving the optimal planning problem of renewable energy sources within distribution grids under uncertainties,pattern,6,10,pdf,2,no,no,"Our primary objective includes minimizing average annual power losses and voltage deviation (VD) while maximizing the yearly aver- age voltage stability index (VSI) within operational constraints. The study considers uncertainties in RES, including fluctuations in wind speed, availability of solar irradiance, temperature variations, and time- varying load demand, based on real historical collected data from the study area over a seasonal planning horizon. The proposed approach is evaluated against several established optimization techniques, includ- ing the well-known Grey Wolf Optimizer (GWO) [27], Harris Hawks optimization (HHO) [28], Chernobyl Disaster Optimizer (CDO) [29], Dingo Optimization Algorithm (DOA) [30], Whale Optimization Algo- rithm (WOA) [31], Black-winged Kite Algorithm (BKA) [32] and the original FLO [33]."
bendriss_novel_2025,A novel improved Frilled Lizard algorithm for solving the optimal planning problem of renewable energy sources within distribution grids under uncertainties,pattern,7,10,pdf,2,no,no,"The study considers uncertainties in RES, including fluctuations in wind speed, availability of solar irradiance, temperature variations, and time- varying load demand, based on real historical collected data from the study area over a seasonal planning horizon. The proposed approach is evaluated against several established optimization techniques, includ- ing the well-known Grey Wolf Optimizer (GWO) [27], Harris Hawks optimization (HHO) [28], Chernobyl Disaster Optimizer (CDO) [29], Dingo Optimization Algorithm (DOA) [30], Whale Optimization Algo- rithm (WOA) [31], Black-winged Kite Algorithm (BKA) [32] and the original FLO [33]. However, the novelty and main achievements of this research are summarized below: 1."
bendriss_novel_2025,A novel improved Frilled Lizard algorithm for solving the optimal planning problem of renewable energy sources within distribution grids under uncertainties,pattern,8,10,pdf,2,no,no,"The proposed approach is evaluated against several established optimization techniques, includ- ing the well-known Grey Wolf Optimizer (GWO) [27], Harris Hawks optimization (HHO) [28], Chernobyl Disaster Optimizer (CDO) [29], Dingo Optimization Algorithm (DOA) [30], Whale Optimization Algo- rithm (WOA) [31], Black-winged Kite Algorithm (BKA) [32] and the original FLO [33]. However, the novelty and main achievements of this research are summarized below: 1. A novel Improved Frilled Lizard (IFLO) Algorithm is developed and proposed to solve the optimal planning problem (OPP) of RESs within the radial distribution grids (RDGs)."
bendriss_novel_2025,A novel improved Frilled Lizard algorithm for solving the optimal planning problem of renewable energy sources within distribution grids under uncertainties,pattern,9,8,abstract,,no,no,"In this research, a new improved frilled lizard optimization algorithm is designed and proposed to address the optimal planning problem of renewable energy sources-based distributed generation within radial distribution grids. The primary objective is to minimize power losses, elevate the voltage profile, and improve voltage stability, formulated as a multi-objective optimization problem."
bendriss_novel_2025,A novel improved Frilled Lizard algorithm for solving the optimal planning problem of renewable energy sources within distribution grids under uncertainties,pattern,10,8,abstract,,no,no,"To this end, we have developed an appropriate probability model to estimate the stochastic power generation from renewable energy sources based on hourly seasonal data, including wind speed, solar irradiance, and ambient temperature collected over a specified time frame and location. The developed improved frilled lizard optimization technique incorporates three distinct strategies: fitness distance balance, quasi-opposite-based learning, and Cauchy mutation, to enhance its searching capabilities and avoid falling into local optimal traps. The suggested improved frilled lizard optimization is successfully applied to identify the optimal locations and rating capacities of solar photovoltaic strings and wind turbines, as well as the power factor of wind turbines."
Zhang20203731,Two-Stage Optimal Operation Strategy of Isolated Microgrid with TSK Fuzzy Identification of Supply Security,pattern,1,13,pdf,2,no,no,"There are mainly three approaches: 1) fuzzy optimization; 2) stochastic optimization; and 3) robust optimization (RO). The ﬁrst one depends mainly on the membership function of the decision- makers’ experience, which can be subjective and not suitable for real-world applications [5], [6]. Stochastic optimization requires probabilistic information, which is either difﬁcult to obtain or not accurate enough for optimization [7], [8]."
Zhang20203731,Two-Stage Optimal Operation Strategy of Isolated Microgrid with TSK Fuzzy Identification of Supply Security,pattern,2,12,pdf,11,no,no,"The system model can be uncertain, multiobjective, and complex coupled, hence, this article proposes a two-stage optimization approach with supply-security identiﬁcation. The TSK fuzzy approach can properly identify the relationship between uncertainty pa- rameters and supply security, and a two-stage optimization strategy can switch ON/OFF power generators to improve the security degree according to three levels of conﬁdence degree, and then, optimize the economic dispatch problem with the known ON/OFF state of the power generators and energy storage units with the GD-MOCDE algorithm; the obtained results can reveal that the proposed method can be an effective way for solving isolated power system problem. C ONCLUSION The uncertainty and complexity of the optimal operation in isolated power system pose a great challenge optimization."
Zhang20203731,Two-Stage Optimal Operation Strategy of Isolated Microgrid with TSK Fuzzy Identification of Supply Security,pattern,3,12,pdf,11,no,no,"The TSK fuzzy approach can properly identify the relationship between uncertainty pa- rameters and supply security, and a two-stage optimization strategy can switch ON/OFF power generators to improve the security degree according to three levels of conﬁdence degree, and then, optimize the economic dispatch problem with the known ON/OFF state of the power generators and energy storage units with the GD-MOCDE algorithm; the obtained results can reveal that the proposed method can be an effective way for solving isolated power system problem. C ONCLUSION The uncertainty and complexity of the optimal operation in isolated power system pose a great challenge optimization. This article proposed a two-stage optimization strategy with a TSK fuzzy identiﬁcation of supply security."
Zhang20203731,Two-Stage Optimal Operation Strategy of Isolated Microgrid with TSK Fuzzy Identification of Supply Security,pattern,4,9,pdf,11,no,no,"With the above-mentioned analysis, optimal operation with supply- security identiﬁcation is a complicated problem. The system model can be uncertain, multiobjective, and complex coupled, hence, this article proposes a two-stage optimization approach with supply-security identiﬁcation. The TSK fuzzy approach can properly identify the relationship between uncertainty pa- rameters and supply security, and a two-stage optimization strategy can switch ON/OFF power generators to improve the security degree according to three levels of conﬁdence degree, and then, optimize the economic dispatch problem with the known ON/OFF state of the power generators and energy storage units with the GD-MOCDE algorithm; the obtained results can reveal that the proposed method can be an effective way for solving isolated power system problem."
